TestNG Annotations:
=====================


-->Suite
   --->Test
         -->Class
               -->TestMethod
                   -->Test


<<------Suite -Run once per Suite------->>
@BeforeSuite - Run before running Test tag in Xml
@AfterSuite  -Run After running  All Test in xml

<<-------Test - Run once for Each Test tag ------->>
@Before Test
@After Test

Note : Here each Test tag class should have the Before Test anno linked (Inheritance)

<<-------Class - Run once for Each class(where it defined) ---->
@BeforeClass
@AfterClass

<<------Method  --Run once for Each Test annotaion in the same class ---->
@BeforeMethod
@AfterMethod
Note : Before/after methods execute -each test (multiple times)

Example :
@BeforeSuite
@BeforeTest
@BeforeClass

@BeforeMethod
@Test1
@AfterMethod

@BeforeMethod
@Test2
@AfterMethod

@AfterClass
@AfterTest
@AfterSuite


===================================
Imp : child class inherit parent class all method - So all method execute
    if Child and parent is having "class " annotation -> parent execute first

 imp : Suite -once should be declared
       Test - can be declare multiple times (All execute but Order is not defined , for order need to use "depends on ")
             -preferred one time
       Class - once per class
       Before method -can be declare multiple times (all executes for all test , but order is not gurentee)
                     -preferred one time in class
       Best use once